<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 95,958 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 95,958 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 95,958 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 64,604 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Thursday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 9,614	   12,128</p>
<p>    Import cargo			86,344	   52,476</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  54,000	 Konpolis	    8/11</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	 Capitan Miranda   6/11</p>
<p>High speed deisel    34,000	 Al-Deerah	    due</p>
<p>High speed deisel    34,954	 Al-Sabiyah	  6/11</p>
<p>High speed deisel    70,000	 Sea Islecity	7/11</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    42,000	 Trade Resolve     9/11</p>
<p>Palm oil		 10,000	 Wawasan Megah     9/11</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
